# Accepted / deliberate findings for the microservice-rust reference example.
# Each entry is the MISCONFIG ID; a trailing comment explains why it is accepted.
#
# KSV-0020 / KSV-0021: runAsUser/runAsGroup must be "> 10000". This is a
#   version-specific Trivy recommendation. The blueprint (deployment D3) and the
#   Dockerfile deliberately use the conventional non-root UID 1000 for a minimal,
#   portable reference image — the security property (non-root, no escalation)
#   is satisfied and does not require an arbitrary host-UID offset.
KSV-0020
KSV-0021
# KSV-0013: the base deployment sets image `settings-service:latest`. The tag is
#   supplied by the deploy step that builds/imports the image into the k3d
#   cluster; a fully-pinned digest is not meaningful for a local reference
#   example where the image is built from source at deploy time (it is NOT a
#   production manifest — see ci-cd.md D10).
KSV-0013
# KSV-0110: base deployment/Job omit metadata.namespace. The k3d overlay
#   (`k8s/overlays/k3d/kustomization.yaml`) sets `namespace: settings`, so the
#   workload does NOT land in `default`; the base manifest is intentionally
#   namespace-agnostic.
KSV-0110
# KSV-0125: third-party infra images (`postgres:16-alpine`, `launchbadge/sqlx-cli`,
#   `otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib`) come from public Docker Hub. They are
#   used only in the local k3d e2e stack, not in a production release path; a
#   private-registry allow-list does not apply to a local reference cluster.
KSV-0125
